# Sources used:
# - Shazam, Frappéy song page (opened 2026-10-20): Frappéy by Weelow, released 3 June 2012 by Bouyon King, LABEL BOUYON MUSIC, as the single Frappéy - Single; genre World, year 2012, language French, tempo 155 BPM; credits: Weelow, performer and songwriter; Wilow Désirade, composer. The page counted about a thousand Shazams at the time it was opened.
# - Wikipedia, Music of Guadeloupe article, Bouyon gwada section (opened 2026-10-20): bouyon is a popular music of Dominica, also known as jump up in Guadeloupe and Martinique; the best known band is WCK, who originated the style in 1988; bouyon gwada grew with Dominican bands touring the French Antilles and with exchanges around the World Creole Music Festival; a popular offshoot within bouyon gwada is bouyon hardcore, characterised by lewd and violent lyrics; popular bouyon gwada musicians include Wee Low, Suppa, Doc J, Yellow gaza. The same list is carried by the reference articles on the music of France and the music of the Lesser Antilles.
# Note on spelling and identity: the streaming record writes the artist name in one word, Weelow; the reference articles write it in two words, Wee Low. This profile treats the two spellings as the same artist on the basis of genre, island and period, and says so openly; no source consulted states the equivalence in so many words. The composer credit Wilow Désirade is printed as a credit only: no source says the artist was born in or comes from La Désirade, and this profile does not claim it. Other artists with similar names in other scenes are not merged with this one.

